# strings.iron expected-scopes reference.
Token               | Scope
--------------------|--------------------------------
"hello"             | string.quoted.double.iron
"line\n"            | string.quoted.double.iron (containing constant.character.escape.iron for \n)
"value is {x}"      | string.quoted.double.iron (containing meta.interpolation.iron for {x})
"hi {f("bob")}"     | nested string.quoted.double.iron inside meta.interpolation.iron
"\{a\} \u{e9}"      | constant.character.escape.iron for \{, \} and \u{...}
"""..."""           | string.quoted.triple.iron

Covers UI-SPEC S6: string.quoted.double.iron, string.quoted.triple.iron,
meta.interpolation.iron (nested), constant.character.escape.iron.

The interpolation pattern uses a begin/end delimiter pair and includes
$self, so string literals nested in an interpolation are scoped as strings
(no nested unbounded quantifiers; safe-regex lint green).
